<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kadıköy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kadıköy is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a> on the Asian shore of the Bosporus, facing the historic peninsula. It occupies the site of ancient Chalcedon, founded by Megarian colonists in the 7th century BCE, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-chalcedon">Council of Chalcedon</a> met in 451. Today it is a busy residential, commercial and cultural centre linked to the European side by ferry and rail.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kad-koy.jpg" alt="Kadıköy" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Starliner · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haydarpasa_train_station_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
